From: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: handle graph-client lifecycle replies

The protected SP11 pull graph addresses GRAPH_START, GRAPH_STOP and
GRAPH_FLUSH through its allocated graph-client port, matching the recovered
Windows transaction.  The DSP therefore returns the basic response to
graph_callback(), not the global APM callback.

Teach the graph callback to complete those lifecycle commands.  The DSP
starts the graph successfully, but Linux otherwise ignores the reply, waits
five seconds, and reports a false timeout.  A retry subsequently receives
AR_EALREADY from pull-ring configuration because the first graph is already
running.

Log the accepted SP11 GRAPH_START boundary so boot evidence distinguishes a
real lifecycle acknowledgment from configuration-only progress.

Signed-off-by: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -1229,6 +1229,9 @@ static int graph_callback(const struct gpr_resp_pkt *data, void *priv, int op)
 		case APM_CMD_SET_CFG:
 		case APM_CMD_GET_CFG:
 		case APM_CMD_REGISTER_MODULE_EVENTS:
+		case APM_CMD_GRAPH_START:
+		case APM_CMD_GRAPH_STOP:
+		case APM_CMD_GRAPH_FLUSH:
 			graph->result.opcode = result->opcode;
 			graph->result.status = result->status;
 			if (result->status)
@@ -1330,9 +1333,13 @@ int q6apm_graph_start(struct q6apm_graph *graph)
 	struct audioreach_graph *ar_graph = graph->ar_graph;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	if (ar_graph->start_count == 0)
+	if (ar_graph->start_count == 0) {
 		ret = audioreach_graph_client_mgmt_cmd(graph,
 						      APM_CMD_GRAPH_START);
+		if (!ret && graph->pull_mode)
+			dev_info(graph->dev,
+				 "SP11 stage GRAPH_START accepted\n");
+	}
 
 	if (!ret)
 		ar_graph->start_count++;
